{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And He gives, bread of distress and water of oppression.</b> For they were in famine, as I explained, and \"water\" is not implied; thus it is, \"and water, what [is] oppression,\" like \"the tent of Sarah his mother\" (Genesis 24:67):" "<b>nor shall it be withdrawn.</b> It shall be far, [so] that it be at the edge of the earth:" "<b>your teachers.</b> In the straight path, and they are Hezekiah and his officers:" "<b>And your eyes.</b> Doubled in meaning, as is the rule:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The verse phrase is parsed as two independent constructs; 'water' is taken as absolute, not construct-bound to the preceding noun, paralleling the syntactic pattern of the Genesis citation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:06.657732920Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}